": "2026-04-18T15:15:58Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "5.\tX wrote a letter to Y in June 1947. The letter starts out expressing X’s deep emotional reaction to the news of the constitutional abolition of a highly discriminatory social practice that had been prevalent in Y’s country for millennia. It acknowledges the leadership role Y and his mentor played in making that abolition happen. X then proceeds to make the case for Y to support the Jewish cause in Palestine. X says: “May I appeal to you, as the leader of a movement of social and national enfranchisement, to recognize in Zionism a similar movement whose realization will add to the peace and progress of the Orient. Free Jewish immigration to Palestine, and the right of the Jews to continue the upholding of their ancient homeland without artificial restrictions, will increase the sum of well being in the world. It is time to make an end to the ghetto status of Jews in Palestine, and to the pariah status of Jews among peoples.” Y was not impressed. He responded to X with measured tact and firmness, rejecting X’s attempt to equate Zionism with the cause Y had championed in his country. X died a few years later, on April 18, 1955. ID X (8 points) and Y (7 points).", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-18T15:16:11Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "Einstein", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-18T15:16:12Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "Nehru", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-18T15:16:14Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Einsteingamdhi", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-18T15:16:15Z", "username": "Srijan Naayak", "text": "Einstein", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-18T15:16